+The default64 full-store encoder stages its final one-to-fifteen-record tail
+in a shared helper and uses one, two, three or four quads. The helper returns
+the final byte count and takes the fixup cursor by value; its caller retains
+no tail staging array or work after that result. Full groups, other modes and
+alternative gather/store paths are unchanged. Record format, encoded bytes,
+offsets/fixups and output-capacity contracts are unchanged.
+
 `x86_target_form_allowed` tests a form including its FS/GS and fixup flags.
 `x86_target_validate` checks both ISA eligibility and `x86_validate`'s operands,
 returning the first failing record index, or the count on success. Initialize
